WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.612 --> 00:00:20.453
next morning the three children decided to walk to town.

2
00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:22.514
Soon they ran into Mabel.

3
00:00:23.495 --> 00:00:25.736
Gerald knew she was going to ask about the ring.

4
00:00:26.737 --> 00:00:29.558
Luckily they'd gotten it back from Eliza the previous night.

5
00:00:30.499 --> 00:00:33.000
Every Friday a market was set up in the square.

6
00:00:33.988 --> 00:00:38.431
Vendors sold chickens, vegetables, toys, and all sorts of interesting things.

7
00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:45.876
buy some flowers for Mademoiselle," suggested Kathleen.

8
00:00:45.896 --> 00:00:49.199
"Yes," agreed Gerald.

9
00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:52.701
"We haven't paid attention to her for the longest time."

10
00:00:53.682 --> 00:00:56.143
The children chose three bunches of carnations.

11
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.488
Then they went back to the school.

12
00:01:05.104 --> 00:01:09.126
Gerald knocked on the door of the sitting room, where Mademoiselle spent all her days.

13
00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.848
The other children gathered behind him.

14
00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:14.909
"With love from all of us."

15
00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.351
Gerald gave the flowers to her.

16
00:01:20.472 --> 00:01:22.493
Mademoiselle kissed him on both cheeks.

17
00:01:30.638 --> 00:01:31.778
"What are you painting?"

18
00:01:32.239 --> 00:01:32.819
asked Jimmy.

19
00:01:32.839 --> 00:01:34.500
"The castle."

20
00:01:35.744 --> 00:01:37.986
"That's very good," said Mabel.

21
00:01:38.006 --> 00:01:40.768
"Are you a friend from town?"

22
00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:42.309
Mademoiselle asked her.

23
00:01:42.329 --> 00:01:49.574
"Actually I live at Yalding Towers," said Mabel, using the castle's formal name.

24
00:01:50.555 --> 00:01:52.576
That name seemed to impress Mademoiselle.

25
00:01:52.596 --> 00:01:56.019
"Are you part of Lord Yalding's family?"

26
00:01:56.039 --> 00:01:59.802
"No, he doesn't have any family.

27
00:02:00.122 --> 00:02:01.042
He's not married.

28
00:02:01.463 --> 00:02:02.884
I'm his housekeeper's niece."

29
00:02:04.704 --> 00:02:06.665
"But you know him, don't you?"

30
00:02:07.206 --> 00:02:08.086
asked Mademoiselle.

31
00:02:08.106 --> 00:02:11.269
"No, I've never seen him.

32
00:02:11.629 --> 00:02:13.450
But he's supposed to be coming soon."

33
00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.512
"Why doesn't he live there?"

34
00:02:17.393 --> 00:02:19.934
Mademoiselle seemed very interested in this man.

35
00:02:19.954 --> 00:02:24.097
"My aunt says he's too poor," said Mabel.

36
00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:30.241
She explained that the castle had originally belonged to Lord Yalding's uncle.

37
00:02:31.322 --> 00:02:35.689
Lord Yalding had wanted to marry a woman, but his uncle had not allowed it.

38
00:02:35.709 --> 00:02:42.272
"She was a ballerina or something," explained Mabel.

39
00:02:43.272 --> 00:02:47.014
When the uncle died, he left his castle to Lord Yalding.

40
00:02:48.015 --> 00:02:49.895
But he left his money to a cousin.

41
00:02:50.916 --> 00:02:54.197
So Lord Yalding didn't have enough money to live at the castle.

42
00:02:55.178 --> 00:02:59.340
Meanwhile the woman Lord Yalding loved was sent away to a convent.

43
00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.581
"Did he ever try to find her?"

44
00:03:08.061 --> 00:03:08.981
asked Mademoiselle.

45
00:03:09.001 --> 00:03:12.322
"Oh yes," said Mabel.

46
00:03:12.342 --> 00:03:15.063
"But there are so many convents."

47
00:03:16.223 --> 00:03:17.643
Her eyes glowed brightly.

48
00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:22.505
"Still, I believe he will find her one day."

49
00:03:23.445 --> 00:03:25.625
Mademoiselle stared silently at Mabel.

50
00:03:25.645 --> 00:03:28.066
"My goodness!"

51
00:03:28.726 --> 00:03:29.586
she said finally.

52
00:03:29.606 --> 00:03:32.927
"You know a lot about Lord Yalding!

53
00:03:33.428 --> 00:03:34.688
You're a very nice girl.

54
00:03:35.396 --> 00:03:36.677
Why don't you stay for lunch?"

55
00:03:38.118 --> 00:03:40.779
Mademoiselle went out to buy some special treats.

56
00:03:44.761 --> 00:03:47.083
Jimmy and Kathleen set the dining room table.

57
00:03:48.103 --> 00:03:50.184
Gerald and Mabel were left in the sitting room.

58
00:03:50.204 --> 00:03:53.646
"You know," Gerald suddenly said.

59
00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:58.169
"It's lucky those burglars didn't go after the jewels in the treasure room."

60
00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:03.712
"I don't think anyone knows about those jewels except the four of us," said Mabel.

61
00:04:04.752 --> 00:04:09.113
"Anyway, if the burglars do know, it'll all come out at the trial."

62
00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:12.594
"There won't be a trial," said Gerald.

63
00:04:12.614 --> 00:04:14.755
"What do you mean?"

64
00:04:14.775 --> 00:04:20.036
"After I told Officer Johnson where to find the silver, I started thinking.

65
00:04:20.416 --> 00:04:22.357
I visited a prison once with my father.

66
00:04:22.757 --> 00:04:23.477
It was awful!"

67
00:04:25.278 --> 00:04:28.659
Gerald didn't want to be responsible for sending someone to prison.

68
00:04:29.639 --> 00:04:33.240
So he had left the burglars a note, warning them about the police.

69
00:04:37.452 --> 00:04:41.555
But he also said if they didn't stop stealing, he'd make sure they went to jail.

70
00:04:44.877 --> 00:04:49.620
"Speaking of stealing," said Mabel, "did you get the ring back from Eliza?"

71
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:54.043
"Yes, but I don't know if it'll make you invisible again."

72
00:04:54.063 --> 00:04:56.005
"Why not?

73
00:04:56.485 --> 00:04:57.726
Did you do something to it?"

74
00:04:58.046 --> 00:04:59.087
Mabel asked sharply.

75
00:04:59.107 --> 00:05:03.250
"No, but it seems to be losing its powers.

76
00:05:04.611 --> 00:05:05.851
You were invisible for 21 hours.

77
00:05:07.096 --> 00:05:10.258
I was invisible for 14, and Eliza for 7.

78
00:05:10.738 --> 00:05:12.499
Next time it might not work at all."

79
00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.600
Mabel shook her head.

80
00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.562
"We don't understand the mystery of that ring yet."
